# WT: the image path in the real app against the fake server, as alexk in Couch Co-op's #general.
#
# The fake server measures an uploaded raster image and makes a thumbnail when its longest side
# exceeds 480 px, exactly as the backend's MediaDimensionsService and ThumbnailService do, and
# every attachment it builds carries width, height and hasThumbnail. This script proves the client
# end to end:
#
#   1. A portrait (600 x 1200) and a panorama (1600 x 300) in one message: the list asks for each
#      picture's /thumbnail (never the full file) and draws two 250-wide boxes at the pictures'
#      own aspects. The thumbnail route is held for a few seconds so the reserved boxes can be
#      photographed before the bytes arrive (`snap 01-boxes-before-load`) and after (`shot 02-loaded`).
#   2. A tiny 64 x 64 picture in its own message has no thumbnail: the list asks for its full file
#      and draws it at its own size.
#   3. Opening the viewer fetches the portrait's full file.
#
# The box sizes are the UI's: a message with several attachments gives each a 250 px cell, so a
# 2:1 portrait is 250 x 500 and a 16:3 panorama is 250 x 46.875. A lone 64 x 64 picture is 64 x 64.

app 1280 800
# Hold the thumbnail route so the boxes can be seen before the pictures load. The upload, message
# and file routes are untouched.
server delay_route "{\"operationId\": \"FileController_getFileThumbnail\", \"ms\": 4000}"
wait idle
click auth-connect
wait core label "Username" within 5
click auth-username
type "alexk"
click auth-password
type "hunter2"
click auth-login
wait core session signed-in
wait core connection connected
wait core channel $ID(cc-general)
wait core rows >= 14
wait core file-ready sc-img-pit within 10
wait idle

# 1. Two large pictures in one message: uploaded, attached, and their boxes reserved.
attach rigs/slice/fixtures/portrait.png
attach rigs/slice/fixtures/panorama.png
type "two pictures"
press enter
wait core sent "two pictures"
wait core attachments "two pictures" 2 within 15
wait core uploads "two pictures" 0
wait core pending-files "two pictures" 0
wait core requests FileUploadController_uploadFile >= 2
wait core requests MessagesController_addAttachment >= 2
# The fake server seeds the scenario's soundboard files (four communities, three sounds each)
# and numbers uploads from there: one message's first two are the 13th and 14th.
snap 01-boxes-before-load
# The boxes' shapes come from the attachment's dimensions, before any pixels arrive.
wait core w7t box "two pictures" portrait.png 250 500 within 15
wait core w7t box "two pictures" panorama.png 250 47 within 15
shot 02-loaded

# 1, continued: each large picture was fetched through /thumbnail, and neither at full size.
expect core w7t thumbnail 0000f11e-0000-4000-8000-00000000000d 1
expect core w7t thumbnail 0000f11e-0000-4000-8000-00000000000e 1
expect core w7t full 0000f11e-0000-4000-8000-00000000000d 0
expect core w7t full 0000f11e-0000-4000-8000-00000000000e 0

# 2. A tiny picture: no thumbnail request, fetched whole, drawn at its own size.
attach rigs/slice/fixtures/tiny.png
type "tiny picture"
press enter
wait core sent "tiny picture"
wait core attachments "tiny picture" 1 within 15
wait core uploads "tiny picture" 0
wait core pending-files "tiny picture" 0
wait core w7t box "tiny picture" tiny.png 64 64 within 15
expect core w7t thumbnail 0000f11e-0000-4000-8000-00000000000f 0
expect core w7t full 0000f11e-0000-4000-8000-00000000000f 1
shot 03-tiny

# 3. Opening the portrait in the viewer fetches the full file; the panorama stays unfetched.
click-row image "two pictures" 0
wait core viewer open
wait idle
shot 04-viewer
expect core w7t full 0000f11e-0000-4000-8000-00000000000d 1
expect core w7t full 0000f11e-0000-4000-8000-00000000000e 0
press escape
wait core viewer closed
